From: BPI-W2 PiKVM <jalen.lin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msd: keep the CD-ROM flag across a disconnect

After a disconnect the drive has no image path, and __update_vd() keeps
the virtual drive's settings -- but it copied the rw flag into cdrom. A
read-only ISO came back as a flash drive on the next connect, and an image
attached read-write came back as a CD-ROM. Fixed upstream after 4.219; this
is the same one-line change.
---
diff --git a/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py b/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py
index da7bab3..38aa18a 100644
--- a/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py
+++ b/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@ class Plugin(BaseMsd):  # pylint: disable=too-many-instance-attributes
         else:
             if self.__state.vd:
                 image = self.__state.vd.image
-                cdrom = self.__state.vd.rw
+                cdrom = self.__state.vd.cdrom
                 rw = self.__state.vd.rw
             if self.__nbd.image:
                 image = self.__nbd.image
